    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bc77a191-dcea-50c3-aa3c-a7c273dedc14",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function is zero at $x=\\pi.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=2n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-1,1].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-27-topic-audit-2/published-probe/17592186176047/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$ and the maximum value is $1$. The range is $[-1,1]$.",
